From d3cf8d88fa50211ea460b30f8ee8847716dbcb65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <2.03348624e+08+yaegerbomb42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:55:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vm): enforce the disk quota on writes and stream-cap
 upload bodies (VM-05, VM-06)

VM-05: uploads never called assertDiskQuota, so an over-quota user could keep
writing and fill the host disk for every tenant.
- assertDiskQuota(user, incomingBytes) now refuses a write whose *projected*
  footprint crosses the quota, not only an already-over workspace.
- The upload route checks the quota with the batch's total bytes before the
  first write; snapshot restore is gated the same way and drops the cached du
  measurement afterwards (the restored volume has a different size).

VM-06: the upload guard read Content-Length (0 for chunked bodies) and the
route sits outside the middleware matcher, so req.formData() buffered an
unbounded body.
- lib/body-limit: capBodyStream() counts bytes as they arrive, errors with
  BodyTooLargeError the moment the cap is crossed and cancels the source, so
  the rest of the upload is never read.
- The upload route feeds that stream to the multipart parser and answers 413
  body_too_large; Content-Length is only an early hint. The cap defaults to
  10 files x 10 MB + 1 MB and SWARM_UPLOAD_MAX_BODY_BYTES may only lower it.

Tests: over-quota upload rejected (nothing written), projected-over-quota
upload rejected, chunked body over the cap cut short with 413, chunked body
under the cap still parsed, restore refused while over quota, cap unit tests.

Refs b13 (VM-05, VM-06)
